    result: 'AUDIT RESOLVED 2026-11-28 (reopened-audit-rerun): no code defect (OI(D) -> session D+2 is correct); the registered claim, the vol-matched range relation replicating on ES, stands. The gamma-specific part is +0.147 [+0.006, +0.289] after return controls (post-hoc, t 2.05), +0.054 [-0.070, +0.178] once implied vol is added (gex-range-iv), and shares its sign with NQ on 82.5% of dates: one market state, not an independent gamma effect. ORIGINAL: VALIDATED as registered. Databento ES options 2020-10 to 2026-10 (quarterly series only), 770 near-surface sessions to 2026-08-20 (lockbox), 199 short / 571 long gamma: vol-matched dDR +0.377 [+0.237, +0.516], Holm p < 0.001, raw +0.208; positive on 4/4 spec cells (+0.25 to +0.38) and both halves (+0.27 / +0.43); +125 placebo -0.006, real above all 130 label shifts; long-gamma DR 0.93, short 1.14. POST-HOC (results seen): short-gamma days follow falls (20-session return -2.7% vs +2.7%, 7% vs 1% below the 60-session high); with trailing returns and drawdown controlled the gamma-specific part is +0.147 [+0.006, +0.289], t 2.05. ES and NQ share the gamma sign on 82.5% of dates, so this is largely the same market state seen through a second book, not an independent confirmation.',
    use: 'G2 is an equity-index range effect, not NQ-only (FX still does not carry it). Say "long gamma has been quieter than a vol-matched baseline, partly because it coincides with rising markets"; never quote +0.38 as the gamma effect (about +0.15 survives return controls, t 2.0, below the |t| >= 3 bar). Range only, no direction; CME book only (no weeklies, no Cboe SPX 0DTE). Research-only: nothing live changes. Next: does gamma add to the shipped SPX500 range lines (own prereg). 2026-11-03: the split-book control (gex-split-book, null) found no book-specific effect where the NQ and ES books disagree, so treat the ~+0.15 as a common-move effect until a strong-book test says otherwise. Implied vol absorbs 64% (ES) / 73% (NQ) of that ~+0.15 (gex-range-iv).',
