    claim: 'In calm-VIX sessions only (implied vol at or below its trailing 252-session median), the short-gamma sessions still run wider than long-gamma at the same trailing vol once the implied-to-realised ratio is in the baseline (SPX500, CME near book, OI(D) to session D+2)',
    result: 'NULL, marginal (registered rule: gate fails and the interval upper end is under +0.10). 770 sessions to 2026-08-20 (lockbox), calm 475 of which 59 short-gamma. b_IV,calm -0.033 [-0.212, +0.099], t -0.42, Holm p 0.67; in stress +0.032 [-0.124, +0.190]; calm minus stress -0.065 [-0.301, +0.136]. IV absorbs more than half of the calm effect (B0 +0.076 to B1 -0.033). The result depends on the calm definition: fixed VIX<20 gives +0.080. MDE 0.26.',
    use: 'Say "calm sessions do not rescue the CME gamma sign on ES: with implied vol controlled the calm-only coefficient is about zero (upper end just under +0.10)". Do not say gamma is informative in calm regimes. The ES CME-book calm question is closed; a calm-only remainder is not ruled out by the fixed-cut sensitivity, only by the registered cut.',
