    claim: 'A daily high-low-close spread estimator (Corwin-Schultz, Abdi-Ranaldo) reproduces the quoted OANDA bid-ask spread closely enough (median error <= 30%, month-to-month Spearman >= 0.5, correct ordering of instruments) to extend cost history beyond the bid/ask M1 window',
    result: 'NULL. 34 instruments with OANDA bid/ask M1 (2016-10 to 2026-08-20, lockbox respected), monthly values vs the quoted London-session spread. Corwin-Schultz: pooled median relative error 952% (95% CI 916% to 982%), median bias 10.7x, within-instrument Spearman 0.29 (0.22 to 0.34), cross-instrument ordering +0.06. Abdi-Ranaldo: relative error 174% (100% to 342%), bias 5.9x, Spearman 0.06, ordering -0.05. Gates (error <= 30%, Spearman >= 0.50, ordering >= 0.80) all fail for both. A random-pairing mirror gives nearly the same agreement (CS Spearman 0.18), so the estimators track the shared volatility cycle, not the spread.',
