    claim: "Rate-of-change stall: after a market's 50-session rate of change was in its own top fifth and has since fallen back to about zero (price flat for 50 sessions after a strong run), the next 20 sessions return less than ordinary sessions of the same market",
    result: "Pre-registered 2026-11-16, scored once on the 2013-01 to 2026-08-21 holdout, 30 daily series (indices, sectors, metals, oil, FX, bonds, bitcoin), 792 de-clustered events, 20-session return in units of a typical 20-session move. Pooled effect +0.050 [-0.046, +0.151] against the bar of -0.15 (the claim needs a FALL); discovery +0.114; halves +0.035 / +0.057; Holm p 0.32. A fall as large as the claim needs is ruled out and the sign is the other way, but the interval's upper edge (+0.1507) sits above the 0.15 bar, so by the registered rule it is UNDERPOWERED, not NULL. MDE 0.12.",
    use: 'Do not say that a flat spell after a run makes a market weaker over the next month: tested on 30 markets over 13 years it does not (the stall is followed by returns about as good as ordinary sessions). The holder-frustration mechanism cannot be seen in prices and is not tested.',
