    claim: 'The right trade at a vol level depends on level, time of day, touch number, approach and path: H1 early Median touches continue, H2 late P75/P90 touches reject, H3 range consumed raises rejection, H4 touch number, H5 fast ladder, H6 a context cell engine fitted 2020-23 makes money net in 2024-26 and beats the same engine on placebo levels',
    result: 'Pre-registered (A1 pre-results race timing; A2 post-hoc demotes ladder/H5 placebo reads). 645k futures (net 2.5 ticks) + 1.1M CFD (gross) touches of High/Low, Close+/-, HL projections at Median/P75/P90, every touch, 2020-2026.08, race +-0.25 line-sigma, 120 min. H1 continue net -0.146R, gross +0.002, line - placebo -0.001 [-0.010, +0.008] NULL; H2 fade net -0.182R, +0.005 [-0.003, +0.014] NULL; H3 +2.7pp rejection, -0.8pp vs placebo NULL; H4 touch 2+ -2.8pp continuation, -0.3pp vs placebo NULL; H5 fast ladder at P90 +12.1pp continuation, +4.4pp vs placebo CONTEXT (momentum; level part not separable, A2); H6 0 of 1,080 cells pass after costs (NULL); before costs engine +0.010R test, = placebo engine (+0.005 [-0.007, +0.017]); CFDs +0.011R but placebo engine -0.002 vs it; ridge model AUC 0.503. Clock changes decisiveness (consolidation 7% NY overlap, 35% after 16:00) not direction. Pointer: P90 07-13 London continuation +3.4/+2.5pp vs placebo, not on CFDs. Graded weight: against a context-aware level engine.',
    use: 'Static vs dynamic level trading makes no difference after costs: context (time, touch n, approach, range used, sequence) moves continuation vs rejection by 1-3pp and the placebo moves the same. Read fast ladders / London-morning P90 as momentum context only. Costs vs a 0.25 sigma move are the binding constraint.',
